    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Functional division of markers",
     "texto": [
      "In the nominative singular, the indefinite article **ein** does not by itself show whether the noun is masculine or neuter. For this reason, the adjective takes the strong ending: **-er** for the masculine (**ein geräumiger Balkon**) and **-es** for the neuter (**ein sonniges Zimmer**). In the feminine singular, since the ending **eine** is already present, the adjective takes the weak form **-e**: **eine moderne Küche**.",
      "Once oblique markers or plural forms appear (**einen**, **einem**, **einer**, **keine**), the adjective passes to the regular ending **-en**: **einen geräumigen Balkon** (masculine accusative), **mit einem modernen Aufzug** (masculine dative), **keine neuen Nachbarn** (plural)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Case and gender",
     "columnas": [
